WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.750
 Hey Marvel fans.

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:01.980
We are here with
David Dastmalchian.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.820
We are on the carpet right
now for Marvel Spider-man

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.840
No Way Home right now.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.490
How excited are you
for this carpet?

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.490
 I'm so excited
being back on a Marvel

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.530
red carpet at a
premiere for a Marvel

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.670
film and it's Spider-man.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.500
And all the exciting
things that are

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.170
about to happen in this movie
that I've just been teased

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.150
by with the trailer, I'm like--

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.830
I know we're all about
to get our minds blown.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.730
But this is like historic
Marvel filmmaking right now

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.710
because there's all these
elements to this new movie

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.250
that we've never
gotten to see before.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.050
 Absolutely.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.729
Is there anyone you're super
excited to see on the carpet

00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:33.750
today?

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.290
 I was really hoping I'd get
to run into Alfred Molina.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.150
I don't know if he's around.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.380
I mean, Tom and Zendaya and
all the incredible stars

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.180
of this movie.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.090
Like I'm big fans of everybody
that is a part of the movie,

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.860
so I'm just geeking
out over everybody.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:48.660
 That's awesome.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.090
Now Spider-man is beloved
by the entire world.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.350
What makes him so relatable
to you and everybody else?

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.300
 It's like when
you were a teenager

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.270
and all of a sudden
everything starts changing

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.520
and the world seems like
it doesn't make any sense,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.010
Peter Parker is the embodiment
of that for all of us.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.590
He's like-- His body starts
changing all these things start

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.720
happening that he has no
control over and all of a sudden

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:10.917
he has this choice to make.

00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:12.550
Like, what am I going to
do with all this change?

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.420
Am I going to do something
to make the world better?

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.820
Or am I going to turn all that
anger and confusion and fear

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.620
into something dark?

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.620
And he continues to inspire
us because over the decades

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.750
Peter Parker and
Spider-man continue

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.100
to rise to the occasion
and be the hero

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.540
that we need them to be.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.680
 I absolutely love that.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.880
Hope, positivity.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:30.810
Enjoy the red carpet.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.960
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:32.980
 Thank you.
Thank you.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.050
Thanks, everybody.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:38.000
[MUSIC PLAYING]

